A||N||4||Taijiguy||SB Chevy rollers in 2.8||||1||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||06-25-2000||11:15 PM||||I read in a V6 performance book that you can retap the rocker studs to 3/8 (or 5/16")studs and install small block Chevy roller rockers. They supposedly sit .030 off center of the valve stem, but that's acceptable. Anyone have experience or firsthand knowledge of this idea?||||reg||1
Z||000001||HYPTNOTiSE||06-25-2000||11:27 PM||||Why not get roller rockers specifically designed for 60 degree v-6 iron head motors?<P>In a few months a company is going to be offering adjustable on the fly varible lift roller rockers. They're a type very similar to the jesels, and at low rpms they have a 1.4 ratio and as Rpm increases the ratio increases to 1.5 then to 1.6 than to 1.7 as you drive. Pretty sweet. <P>I'm using Cam Cams roller tiped rockers. Stock type design and no poly locks to come loose later casuing you to have to re adjust the valves.  Id stay away from 1.6 rockers if i had to do it all over. the minimal increse in hp is not worth the wear to the guides.  especially since you have a .480 lift cam, that's huge! Mines .454 .480 split lift.  What's you're duration at .050? Mines 204/216.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||06-25-2000||11:54 PM||||My primary thought was initially about cost. From what I've seen for the same price as stamped rollers for the V6, you can get cast rollers for the small block. Thus the advantage of using sb rockers.<BR>I just verified the specs on my cam, I was off, the lift is actually Intake.443 Exh .465 lift @ 288/298 duration. 112 overlap. Yours looks like the compucam specs. This cam has a monster lope at 1,100 rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||06-26-2000||12:03 AM||||mines 260/272 or at .050 it's 204/214 with .454/.480 lift.and 112 lobe seperation. Are you running a stock computer with that cam, i'd be very very suprised if you could run a cam with such duration on the street with the stock computer.  My cam is supposedly the largest cam compliant with the stock computer.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||06-26-2000||08:06 AM||||Yep, it's got the stock brain with an ADS Strip-Chip, (for sale soon)The cam does tend to confuse the MAP sensor since the vacuum jumps around so much. It still runs great, but I'm in the process of yanking all the injection stuff anyway. Going to put either a 4bbl or a custom setup with two Holley/Weber 2100 series carbs. I've never been a big fan of all that flash and fashio anyway. Give me a couple of great big fire breathing Carbs to aspirate my machine! (I think maybe those computers are just another way for "Big Brother" to monitor your actions....it probably sends a signal showing your speed, direction, and thoughts to a master computer someplace in Arizona where they store all that stuff to use against you later in life!)<P>Taijiguy &lt;--The new Conspiracy Theorist  (Hah!)<p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 06-26-2000).]||||reg||1
